From 296d2496838d2820d07329e36bea970a67efc5a5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:59:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 235/241] resolve: a glob import only sees items visible from
 its module

wasmparser 0.244.0 (tree-sitter-cli 0.27.1) stopped in use resolution:

    readers/core/types.rs:23-24 error:0: Unable to resolve `use` target crate::types::CoreTypeId

The root has `types` only through globs: `pub use crate::readers::*`
(readers.rs `pub use self::{component, core}::*`, each with a PRIVATE
`mod types;` plus `pub use self::types::*`) and, later, `pub use
crate::validator::*` (`pub mod types`, which has CoreTypeId).

Resolve_Use_GetBinding_Mod's glob search looked the name up in the
glob's target module with no visibility test, so the first glob handed
the root readers::component's private `types`, and the second was never
consulted (merge_from keeps the first binding).

rustc's glob imports only items visible from the importing module. The
module lookup takes a `glob_vis` flag now: on behalf of a glob from
`source_mod_path`, an item not visible from there is skipped (the same
test the import loop already applies to `use` items). Direct lookups are
unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/resolve/use.cpp | 17 ++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/resolve/use.cpp b/src/resolve/use.cpp
index 318f7d17..ab4a58ee 100644
